1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,441
This is Dongmyo, in Seoul. Hundreds of street stalls.

2
00:00:09,441 --> 00:00:13,142
No signs, no addresses, and every piece is one of a kind.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,846
You spot a jacket you love. An hour later, which stall was it?

4
00:00:17,846 --> 00:00:19,619
And which of your forty photos?

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,923
Will it go with the jeans you already own?

6
00:00:22,923 --> 00:00:24,288
You can't try that on here.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,447
And the shirt two stalls down.

8
00:00:27,447 --> 00:00:29,148
Would it work with that jacket?

9
00:00:29,148 --> 00:00:30,905
Walk away, and it might be gone.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,903
Meet Ibo. Find it, try it on, and walk back, with Meta's models.

11
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,083
Turn on shopping mode and just snap.

12
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:43,937
Every photo keeps the spot where you took it.

13
00:00:43,937 --> 00:00:49,644
PE-Core indexes each photo right on your phone, and Muse Spark describes every storefront.

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,541
Later, just ask.

15
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,395
“Find the blue jacket in the second shop.”

16
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,708
Muse Voice Transcribe turns your voice into text.

17
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:03,768
Muse Spark plans the search with tool calls.

18
00:01:03,768 --> 00:01:08,915
It checks your trips, narrows to the right shop, and searches your photos.

19
00:01:08,915 --> 00:01:11,419
Then SAM 3.1 outlines every garment.

20
00:01:11,419 --> 00:01:12,601
Best match first.

21
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,269
Tap the jacket and save it.

22
00:01:17,269 --> 00:01:21,396
Flea markets have no product photos, so your photo becomes one.

23
00:01:21,396 --> 00:01:26,375
If SAM missed something, EdgeTAM cuts it out on the phone with a single tap.

24
00:01:26,375 --> 00:01:29,192
And the piece remembers where you found it.

25
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,670
Now, will it work with what you own?

26
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:37,328
Add your jeans from your wardrobe, or pieces saved from other stalls. Up to five.

27
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:44,249
Before anything leaves your phone, your face and hair are masked on the device.

28
00:01:44,249 --> 00:01:48,016
Only that masked photo and the garment cutouts go to Muse Image.

29
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,347
Your face is put back on the phone.

30
00:01:55,347 --> 00:01:58,573
If it can't be done cleanly, the look is shown without it.

31
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:08,760
One tap, and Ibo walks you back to the spot where you took the photo.

32
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,689
Street stalls aren't on any map.

33
00:02:10,689 --> 00:02:15,211
Your photo is the address. Near the end, check the storefront, and confirm.

34
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,932
One of a kind pieces. No signs.

35
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:24,576
No fitting rooms. Every flea market has this problem.

36
00:02:24,576 --> 00:02:27,808
Ibo lets you find it, try it on, and walk back.

37
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,395
Built this week: the Ibo app, its relay, and all product code. Pre-existing:

38
00:02:36,395 --> 00:02:45,694
the Astryx design system, the Capacitor template, a vendored UI kit for the prototype, and Meta's open EdgeTAM and PE-Core weights.
